Subject: [PATCH] js: drop the JS shell from the build (iOS)

The standalone JS shell (js/src/shell) uses system() and fork(), which iOS
marks __API_UNAVAILABLE — hard compile errors. The shell is a dev/test tool;
embedders (gjs) only need libmozjs / libjs_static. Drop "shell" from DIRS.

Note "shell" is grouped with "rust" under the same `if not JS_DISABLE_SHELL`;
"rust" (jsrust/mozglue) IS needed by the library, so keep it — remove only the
"shell" entry rather than the whole conditional (which would also orphan the
nested FUZZING_INTERFACES block).

--- a/js/src/moz.build
+++ b/js/src/moz.build
@@ -50,7 +50,6 @@
 if not CONFIG["JS_DISABLE_SHELL"]:
     DIRS += [
         "rust",
-        "shell",
     ]

     TEST_DIRS += [
